   "status": "answered",
   "answer": "[NISTIR 8312] defines four principles of explainable artificial intelligence:\n\n1. Meaningful: A system provides explanations that are understandable to the intended consumer(s).\n\n2. Explanation Accuracy: An explanation correctly reflects the reason for generating the output and/or accurately reflects the system's process.\n\n3. Knowledge Limits: A system only operates under conditions for which it was designed and when it reaches sufficient confidence in its output.\n\n4. Contextual Factors Considerations: The principles allow for defining the contextual factors to consider for an explanation, paving the way forward to measure explanation quality.",
